    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30402" root="علو" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلْوٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُلْوٌ</span> in five places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>A high,</i> or
<i>an elevated, state of the base,</i> or <i>foundation, of a
building.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And you say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخَذَهُ عَلْوًا</span>,
meaning (assumed tropical:)  <i>He took him,</i> or <i>it, by force.</i> (K,
TA.) See also the next but one of the preceding
paragraphs.

